---
import LegalLayout from "@layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy | Moka Bio"
  description="How Moka Bio, Inc. collects, uses, and protects personal information on moka.bio, including GDPR, CCPA, Mexico, Brazil, and Argentina rights."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updatedLabel="Last updated"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
  <div class="legal-notice">
    <p class="legal-notice-heading">Scope of This Policy</p>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy applies exclusively to personal information collected through
      the <strong>moka.bio</strong> website (the "Site"). It does not govern the processing
      of data in connection with the Moka Bio platform, research services, or partnerships,
      which is governed by the individual written agreements executed with each client or partner.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>1. Who We Are / Data Controller</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Moka Bio, Inc.</strong> is a corporation organized under the laws of the
      State of Delaware, United States of America ("Moka Bio", "we", "us", "our").
      Moka Bio is the data controller responsible for the personal information described
      in this Policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      For any privacy inquiry or request, contact us at:
      <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Information you provide directly</h3>
    <p>
      Our contact form prepares an email in your own email application. We only receive
      the information if you send that email. It may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name</li>
      <li>Your company or organization</li>
      <li>Your email address</li>
      <li>Your phone number (optional)</li>
      <li>The type of inquiry (platform demo, R&amp;D service, or other)</li>
      <li>The content of your message</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We also receive any information you include when you write to us directly by email.
    </p>

    <h3>Information collected automatically (only with your consent)</h3>
    <p>
      If you accept analytics cookies, we use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to collect
      technical and usage data, including:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pages visited and navigation path</li>
      <li>Time spent on each page</li>
      <li>Device type, browser, and operating system</li>
      <li>Approximate geographic location (country and city level)</li>
      <li>Referral source (how you arrived at the Site)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you reject analytics cookies, Google Analytics is not loaded and none of this data
      is collected. According to Google, Google Analytics 4 does not log or store IP addresses.
      We do not combine analytics data with the information you send us by email.
    </p>

    <h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
    <p>
      We do not request sensitive personal data such as health information, financial data,
      biometric data, racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious beliefs, or trade
      union membership through this Site. Please do not include such data in your messages.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>3. Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Responding to your inquiry</strong> — to answer your message, schedule a demo,
        or prepare a proposal for a service you request. Legal basis under the GDPR: steps taken
        at your request prior to entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and our legitimate
        interest in responding to business inquiries (Art. 6(1)(f)). Under the LGPD, the equivalent bases are Art. 7, V and IX.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Website analytics</strong> — to understand how visitors use the Site and improve
        its content. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR; Art. 7, I LGPD), which you can withdraw at
        any time through the "Cookie settings" link in the footer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal obligations</strong> — to comply with applicable laws and respond to
        lawful requests from authorities (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR; Art. 7, II LGPD).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal data, use it for behavioral advertising, or make automated
      decisions about you. We will not send you marketing communications unless you ask us to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Inquiry data</strong> is retained for up to 36 months from the date of your last
      communication, or for as long as necessary to maintain a business relationship with you,
      whichever is longer. It is then deleted unless a legal obligation requires longer retention.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Analytics data</strong> is retained in Google Analytics for the retention period
      configured in our account, which does not exceed 14 months, after which Google deletes it
      automatically.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We only share it in the
      following cases:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google LLC</strong> — as an analytics provider, only if you accept analytics
        cookies, under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>
        and Google's data processing terms.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email and productivity providers</strong> — which process correspondence on our
        behalf as data processors, bound by contractual data protection obligations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal authorities</strong> — when required by applicable law, court order, or
        governmental authority, or when necessary to protect the rights, property, or safety of
        Moka Bio, its clients, or the public.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Business transfers</strong> — in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale
        of all or substantially all of Moka Bio's assets, subject to equivalent privacy protections.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>6. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Moka Bio is incorporated in the United States. Your data may be stored and processed on
      servers located in the United States or in other countries outside your country of residence.
    </p>
    <p>
      For transfers from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Brazil, or other jurisdictions
      that require it, we rely on appropriate safeguards, such as the Standard Contractual Clauses
      approved by the European Commission or equivalent mechanisms. You may request information
      about these safeguards at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>7. Cookies and Your Choice</h2>
    <p>
      When you first visit the Site, we ask whether you accept analytics cookies. Google Analytics
      cookies are only set if you accept. We do not use advertising, remarketing, or social media cookies.
    </p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
      <table class="legal-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Provider</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>moka-analytics-consent</td>
            <td>Moka Bio (local storage)</td>
            <td>Remembers your cookie choice. Required for the Site to respect your decision.</td>
            <td>Until you delete it</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>_ga</td>
            <td>Google Analytics</td>
            <td>Distinguishes visitors (only with consent)</td>
            <td>2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>_ga_*</td>
            <td>Google Analytics</td>
            <td>Maintains session state (only with consent)</td>
            <td>2 years</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      You can change your choice at any time using the <strong>"Cookie settings"</strong> link in
      the footer. You can also delete cookies through your browser settings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>8. Your Rights — EEA and UK (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
    <p>If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15).</li>
      <li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data (Art. 16).</li>
      <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data, subject to legal retention obligations (Art. 17).</li>
      <li><strong>Restrict</strong> processing in certain circumstances (Art. 18).</li>
      <li><strong>Data portability</strong> in a structured, machine-readable format (Art. 20).</li>
      <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21).</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, without affecting prior processing.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with your national data protection authority or, in the UK,
        the Information Commissioner's Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will respond within one month, extendable by two further months for complex requests.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>9. Your Rights — California (CCPA / CPRA)</h2>
    <p>If you are a California resident, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Know</strong> the categories and specific pieces of personal information we collect, use, and disclose.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> personal information we have collected from you, subject to certain exceptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate personal information.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out of sale or sharing</strong> — we do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.</li>
      <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will respond within 45 days, extendable to 90 days where necessary.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>10. Your Rights — Mexico (LFPDPPP)</h2>
    <p>
      Under the Federal Law on the Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties (published
      March 20, 2025), you may exercise your rights of <strong>Access, Rectification, Cancellation,
      and Opposition (ARCO)</strong>, and revoke your consent, by writing to
      <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a> with your name, the right you wish to
      exercise, and a description of the data concerned.
    </p>
    <p>
      We will communicate our decision within 20 business days of receiving your request and, if
      it is granted, make it effective within the following 15 business days. The competent
      authority is the Secretaría Anticorrupción y Buen Gobierno.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>11. Your Rights — Brazil (LGPD)</h2>
    <p>Under the Brazilian General Data Protection Law (Law No. 13,709/2018), you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirmation that we process your data, and access to it.</li>
      <li>Correction of incomplete, inaccurate, or outdated data.</li>
      <li>Anonymization, blocking, or deletion of unnecessary or excessive data, or data processed in breach of the LGPD.</li>
      <li>Portability of your data to another provider.</li>
      <li>Deletion of data processed with your consent, and revocation of that consent.</li>
      <li>Information about the entities with which we share your data, and about the possibility of not giving consent and its consequences.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our channel for data subject requests is <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
      We will respond to requests for confirmation or access within 15 days. You may also file a
      complaint with the Autoridade Nacional de Proteção de Dados (ANPD).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>12. Your Rights — Argentina (Law 25,326)</h2>
    <p>
      You may request access to your personal data free of charge at intervals of no less than six
      months, unless a legitimate interest is demonstrated. We will respond to access requests within
      10 business days, and to requests for rectification, updating, or deletion within 5 business
      days, by writing to <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Agencia de Acceso a la Información Pública, as the control authority of Law No. 25,326,
      is empowered to handle complaints and claims filed by those whose rights are affected by
      non-compliance with personal data protection rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>13. Other Jurisdictions</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, local law may grant you additional rights. Where mandatory local
      law grants rights broader than those described here, those rights apply. To exercise any of
      them, contact <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>14. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your personal data
      against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction, including access
      controls and encryption in transit.
    </p>
    <p>
      No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
      absolute security. If a security incident is likely to affect your rights, we will notify the
      competent authorities and, where required, the affected individuals, as required by applicable law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>15. Minors</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for business professionals and is not directed at individuals under 16
      years of age (or the age of digital consent in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect
      data from minors. If you believe we have received such data, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>16. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Policy to reflect changes in our practices, technology, or legal
      requirements. We will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page and, for
      material changes, display a notice on the Site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>17. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Moka Bio, Inc.</strong><br />
      Delaware, United States of America<br />
      <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
